 "id": "bigville_speech_decide",
 "version": "1.0.0",
 "depends_on": [],
 "self_load_only": true,
 "description": "BIGVILLE RUNG 2/3 (block 278000) -- EMERGENT SPEECH: the DECISION to speak, not a schedule. An utterance is an EMERGENT ACTION -- at an encounter/trade an agent DECIDES whether/to-whom/what-KIND to speak OR to STAY SILENT by reading its held Bond(A->B) (rung 1) + conversational norms + affect, with NO clock term. sp_choose_utterance EXTENDS af_choose_action into a speech-act Argmax over a GLOBAL SpeechOption menu that INCLUDES stay_silent: value = occasion x relationship x goal x affect_gain - face_cost - civil_inattention, over a per-agent loquacity_threshold. Adjacency (a pending FPP) is the strongest norm term (routes to the matching option -> a greeting begets a greeting). KIND is DERIVED from adjacency then the Bond's relational affect. sp_noticeable_absence mints a LEGIBLE snub node when an obligation goes unmet (non-response is a MOVE, Schegloff). sp_set_chosen_loudness feeds arousal into the LANDED lo_choose_loudness (delivery gate). FALSIFIER: zeroing the coupling gains collapses the decision to ONE fixed kind regardless of Bond = the OLD forced schedule (mirrors af_choose_action's affect_gain). Composes existing DSL Terms only; ZERO new Rust. OFF by default.",
 "nodes": [],
 "edges": [],
 "productions": [],
 "concepts": [],
