   "name": "sp_noticeable_absence",
   "batch": false,
   "comment": "NON-RESPONSE IS A MOVE (Schegloff official absence, SCIENCE \u00a71.3/\u00a73.3): when a conditionally-relevant obligation existed (obligation==1, a pending FPP was directed at A) and the chosen code is silence (0), MINT a legible NoticeableAbsence node and wire the snubbed target -notices-> it, so other agents' ToM/affect can read the snub. Silence is a first-class output here, NOT the mere non-firing of a rule. Mint-once (absence_minted guard).",
